# Deploy-safety FLOOR — secure-build baseline (Sub-cycle C) — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/deploy-safety-floor-gate-primitives.md` §6 Sub-cycle C —
the always-on secure-build FLOOR for the artifact loam PRODUCES (Tilth
`F-SECURE-BUILD-BASELINE`). A distinct surface from securing loam itself:
the three guarantees are on for every build by default.

Scope (plan §6 Sub-cycle C): NEW component
`framework/secure-build-baseline/` + an additive EXTEND of the sealed
`framework/safety-layer/` secret_pattern_guard.

  - AC.SBB.1 — secrets-never-committed at the commit/push boundary. The
    safety-layer `secret_pattern_guard` is EXTENDED (strictly additively)
    with a staged-diff scan: a `git commit` / `git push` boundary command
    triggers a scan of the content the boundary would publish (the staged
    diff for commit, the unpushed range for push) for the same CONTENT
    credential shapes — catching a secret embedded in a FILE, not just on
    the command line, and firing for any repo loam BUILDS (read via `git`
    against the command's cwd), not only loam's own. No secret value is
    echoed (redacted token shape only). The new branch and helpers change
    none of the existing CONTENT/FILE logic and none of the guard's
    fail-OPEN fault policy: a `git` read failure yields no match, so the
    inbound-paste path's `D-SECHK.FAIL-OPEN` behavior is unchanged (plan
    §8 HALT honored — verified by the fail-open regression suites).
  - AC.SBB.2 — dependency-hygiene audit gate. On a build/publish command
    in a supported ecosystem (Node/Next, Python) the floor runs the
    ecosystem's OWN audit (`npm audit` / `pip-audit`) through an
    injectable runner and gates on a configured severity floor:
    block-or-surface per strictness on a vuln at/above floor, a clean
    audit passes silently, and an UNAVAILABLE audit tool is surfaced
    honestly (never reported clean for an audit that did not run — Lens 0).
    Composes on the ecosystem's vuln DB; loam re-implements none (Lens 1).
  - AC.SBB.3 — artifact-cleanliness. `gitignore_template` is the single
    source of truth for the floor `.gitignore` (harness runtime state —
    `.scratch/`, per-workspace memory queues, tracker `*.sqlite` — plus
    secrets / `.env`). `artifact_sweep` is the runtime enforcement: on a
    broad-stage command (`git add -A` / `.` / `commit -a`) it inspects the
    target repo for runtime-state / secret paths that are present and NOT
    git-ignored (would enter the artifact) and blocks-or-surfaces.
  - AC.SBB.4 — the baseline is a NON-tunable floor. The three guarantees
    are on for every build by default; the ONLY tunable is each
    guarantee's strictness (block vs surface, via
    `<workspace>/.loam/secure-build.yaml`); `secret-commit` is NOT among
    the tunables — `resolve_strictness` ignores any config attempt to
    downgrade it and the floor stays at BLOCK.
  - AC.COV.1 — catalogue coverage. FM.SECRET-LEAK is enriched with the
    AC.SBB.1 staged-diff extension; FM.VULN-DEPENDENCY-SHIPPED (AC.SBB.2)
    and FM.ARTIFACT-LEAKS-RUNTIME-STATE (AC.SBB.3) are added — all
    `default_on: YES`, `class: floor`, with guard_refs that resolve
    against the real tree. The companion `docs/design/protection-matrix.md`
    is regenerated; `loam guards` reports all three `[ok]`, zero
    divergence, and NO new floor gap (gap count unchanged).

Lens 1 (compose, don't re-derive): the dependency audit shells out to the
ecosystem's own tool; the secret-at-commit guard reuses the safety-layer's
sealed CONTENT-pattern set (`all_content_patterns`) rather than minting a
second pattern catalogue.

